+[para]
+
+Option names follow the Tk conventions: an option name must begin with
+a hyphen, and must not contain upper case letters or spaces.  Thus
+[const -transformbefore] is a valid option name, but
+[const transformBefore] and [const -transformBefore] are not.  (The
+option's resource and class names, which are used with
+[sectref "THE TK OPTION DATABASE"], may contain upper case letters;
+see [sectref "What are option resource and class names?"] or
+the [cmd option] statement in the Snit man page.)
+
